# 9. HTTP Security Check

A defensive tool can inspect an authorized HTTP response for security headers.

Examples:

- Content-Security-Policy
- X-Content-Type-Options
- Strict-Transport-Security
- Referrer-Policy

The absence of a header does not automatically mean the application is vulnerable, but it can identify a configuration improvement.

